---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

export const prerender = true;

const description =
  "Bad Gifts uses affiliate links. A commission does not raise the price you pay, and we are not the seller.";
const site = Astro.site;
if (!site) throw new Error("site missing");

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Affiliate disclosure",
  url: new URL(Astro.url.pathname, site).href,
  description,
};
---

<BaseLayout title="Affiliate disclosure" description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">The fine print, in a normal voice</p>
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure.</h1>
    <p>
      Bad Gifts links to other stores. Some of those links are affiliate links. If you buy through
      one, the merchant's program may pay us a commission. That commission does not raise the price
      you pay at checkout.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not the seller. Stock, shipping, returns, and the price on the day you order live on
      the merchant site and can change after we look. A price note is printed only when it was
      checked against a real price. If you do not see one, we did not have a price worth printing.
      We do not guess.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every buy button uses <code>rel="sponsored nofollow noopener"</code> and opens in a new tab.
      A short version of this disclosure sits next to the button.
    </p>
    <p>
      Merchants we expect to link include Amazon, Etsy, AliExpress, and other shops. The gift page
      names which one the button goes to.
    </p>
    <h2>Amazon, when there is actually an account</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not enrolled in Amazon Associates. Amazon requires associates to show a sentence
      like “As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.” Add that sentence here after
      an account is approved. It is not a claim this shop can make yet.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sample entries in the repo are marked <code>draft: true</code> and point at placeholder URLs.
      Production builds leave them out.
    </p>
    <p>This page is a plain-language disclosure, not legal advice.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
